# CODEOWNERS — who reviews what.
#
# GitHub evaluates these lines top-to-bottom and the LAST match wins, so the
# broad default comes first and every tightening follows it.
#
# One maintainer, stated plainly
# ==============================
# @DuqueOM is the only maintainer. Every rule below therefore names the same
# handle, and this file distributes no review today. What it distributes is
# meaning: it records where the ownership boundaries actually fall, so a
# second maintainer can be added one boundary at a time — security and ADRs
# first — instead of all at once by editing a single `*` line.
#
# The consequence a fork must know before relying on this: with one owner, a
# branch-protection rule requiring an approving review from a code owner can
# only ever be satisfied by the author. Adopters under separation-of-duties
# obligations (SOC 2, HIPAA, financial services) must replace this file with
# their own handles before calling the repository reviewed.

# Default owner — everything not matched more specifically below.
*                               @DuqueOM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream-owned: generated, not authored here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `services/` is scaffolded from ml-service-template by copier and the template
# is authoritative for every service-level concern — serving loop, container,
# probes, K8s manifests, supply chain (ADR-003). A fix made here is a local
# patch, and a local patch is how a consumer becomes a fork without deciding
# to. Reviewers: send the change upstream, then `copier update`. The only
# edits that belong in this tree are the ones copier itself produced.
/services/                      @DuqueOM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agentic surface: one canonical store, four generated adapters
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `agentic/` holds the rules, skills and workflows. The per-tool trees below
# are RENDERED from it by scripts/sync_agentic_adapters.py — pointers, not
# sources. Editing one of them makes the same policy say two things, and
# `sync_agentic_adapters.py --check` fails the build when it does. A review
# that sees a hand-edited adapter should ask for the canonical body instead.
/agentic/                       @DuqueOM
/.claude/                       @DuqueOM
/.cursor/                       @DuqueOM
/.codex/                        @DuqueOM
/.devin/                        @DuqueOM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Governance and decisions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An ADR is never deleted or renumbered — a wrong decision is superseded so
# the reasoning survives, and the coherence gate checks that against git
# history rather than the index.
/AGENTS.md                      @DuqueOM
/CLAUDE.md                      @DuqueOM
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @DuqueOM
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md             @DuqueOM
/SECURITY.md                    @DuqueOM
/LICENSE                        @DuqueOM
/NOTICE                         @DuqueOM
/docs/decisions/                @DuqueOM
/docs/governance/               @DuqueOM
/docs/PROJECT_CONTRACT.md       @DuqueOM
/docs/EXPORTING.md              @DuqueOM

# Derived documents. Review the generator and the inputs, never the diff —
# these are rewritten from the filesystem by their scripts, and a hand-edited
# tick in a status table is exactly the defect the generation exists to stop.
/docs/architecture/             @DuqueOM

# Append-only audit trail. Entries are added by scripts/audit_record.py; a
# diff that modifies or removes an existing line is the finding.
/ops/audit.jsonl                @DuqueOM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The gates
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These scripts decide whether anything else can merge, so they are the one
# place where a silently weakened check is invisible. Thresholds live in
# scripts/check_thresholds.py and may rise, not fall.
/scripts/                       @DuqueOM
/tests/                         @DuqueOM
/.pre-commit-config.yaml        @DuqueOM
/.github/                       @DuqueOM
/.github/workflows/             @DuqueOM
/.gitleaks.toml                 @DuqueOM
/codecov.yml                    @DuqueOM
/Makefile                       @DuqueOM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared libraries — the blast radius is every project at once
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A change to a public API in `libs/` crosses a boundary and is at least
# CONSULT. `serving-core` additionally holds the seam against the template: it
# may hold what the platform adds *around* a generated service, never the
# serving loop itself (ADR-003).
/libs/                          @DuqueOM
/libs/data-contracts/           @DuqueOM
/libs/feature-defs/             @DuqueOM
/libs/llm-core/                 @DuqueOM
/libs/ml-core/                  @DuqueOM
/libs/serving-core/             @DuqueOM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verticals and their generator
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Projects are generated from `templates/project/`, so a change to the
# template reaches every future vertical while a change under `projects/` is
# local to one. `docs/PROJECT_CONTRACT.md` states what each must satisfy.
/projects/                      @DuqueOM
/templates/project/             @DuqueOM
/copier.yml                     @DuqueOM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Platform — the paths that touch real infrastructure
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform, cluster manifests and network policy are the changes with a cloud
# bill and a blast radius outside the repository. Policies are default-deny;
# widening one is a security review, not a config tweak.
/platform/terraform/            @DuqueOM
/platform/kubernetes/           @DuqueOM
/platform/policies/             @DuqueOM
/platform/gitops/               @DuqueOM
/platform/observability/        @DuqueOM
/platform/local/                @DuqueOM

# Orchestration runs on a schedule, so a defect here surfaces at 03:00 rather
# than in review.
/orchestration/                 @DuqueOM

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependency and release surface
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/pyproject.toml                 @DuqueOM
/uv.lock                        @DuqueOM
/VERSION                        @DuqueOM
/CHANGELOG.md                   @DuqueOM
